    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Reads the webhook body: { question: \"...\" } and builds the agent prompt.\nconst body = $input.first().json.body ?? {};\nconst question = (body.question || body.q || '').trim();\nif (!question) {\n  throw new Error('Missing \"question\" in request body. Send {\"question\": \"...\"}');\n}\nconst prompt = `AQUASENTINEL USER QUERY\\n\\nQuestion: ${question}\\n\\nUse the available tools to gather evidence from the mock backend, reason over it, and answer the question. End with a clear recommendation if relevant.`;\nreturn [{ json: { prompt } }];\n"
      },
      "id": "prep-5c709b9686be",
      "name": "Prepare Agent Prompt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -540,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.prompt }}",
        "hasOutputParser": false,
        "needsFallback": false,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are the AquaSentinel water-quality agent. You investigate anomalies and answer questions about sensor data using four tools:\n\n- get_current_readings(node_id): current sensor values for a node\n- get_historical_readings(node_id): recent history for a node\n- get_anomaly_event(event_id): details of a specific anomaly event\n- get_sensor_status(node_id): sensor health/status for a node\n\nYou are event-triggered: only use the tools you actually need. Do not fabricate data — if a tool returns no data, say so. Always reason explicitly: Observation -> Inference -> Uncertainty. End your final answer with a \"Recommendation:\" section.",
          "maxIterations": 8,
          "returnIntermediateSteps": false,
          "passthroughBinaryImages": true,
          "enableStreaming": true
        }
      },
      "id": "agent-740c9950d826",
      "name": "AquaSentinel Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        -360,
        0
      ]
    },
